<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Potchefstroom</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Potchefstroom is a city in North West province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, on the Mooi River. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-hendrik-potgieter">Andries Hendrik Potgieter</a> in 1838, it was the first European town north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaal-river">Vaal River</a> and the first capital of the South African Republic until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> replaced it in 1860. It is now a university town, home to a campus of North-West University.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/potchefstroom.jpg" alt="Potchefstroom" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leo za1 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Town_Hall,_Potgieter_Street,_Potchefstroom-001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
